<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila grimshawi Turing wavelength at 2.8 µm (detail) — MorphoEval overall 88.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three pass-1 remediation items. The comparison figure now plots λ_c against δ from 9 to 20 (monotone lengthening; grimshawi at δ = 16.3186, λ = 2.766 µm). Sobel-orientation KS between the masked gallery specimen and the spiral is 0.0418; the zero-arm ablation KS is 0.0191, so orientation distance alone does not rank the spiral first. The full CV score does: the zero-arm ablation, which is not histogram-matched, scores CV 71.4 against 93.8 for the spiral (drop 22.4). Specimen Otsu fraction is referenced to that ablation, not to a copy of itself. Dispersion growth Pearson r remains 0.99974. Chronoseries at 0 Ma, same kinetics: ficusphila 2.512 µm, guttifera 2.629 µm, grimshawi 2.766 µm. Residual limit: the canonical image is the project gallery spiral, not a 2.8 µm wing micrograph, and Lean was not executed because no Lean binary is installed. Overall 88.2/100 (faithfulness 88.4, reproducibility 87.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 89, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 89, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 521128 B, 1144×1232 px, artifact_sha256 5e740d6d5a9e0aac8a8b14d87da6804c95ee90ed200e910fb7305856407c55fd (sha256 5e740d6d5a9e0aac8a8b14d87da6804c95ee90ed200e910fb7305856407c55fd), spec_fingerprint e889fa230e849b3a3849aace67edfdc63e0c1f6e6b4678385e1b298ef5811b4a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e889fa230e849b3a3849aace67edfdc63e0c1f6e6b4678385e1b298ef5811b4a; artifact_sha256: 5e740d6d5a9e0aac8a8b14d87da6804c95ee90ed200e910fb7305856407c55fd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=ac4d59314c82a9c0..., datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=4ea3740942a29423..., datasets/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=ebf2b96514b75c28...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) supply the instability and the kinetics. | Edwards et al. (2007) and Werner et al. (2010) are the picture-wing and guttifera Wingless sources. They do not measure a 2.765 µm wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Fastest-mode calibration, numerical growth fit, δ sweep, chronoseries order, orientation KS, Otsu fractions, and the zero-arm ablation. | Spiral render with the specimen radial envelope and a melanin colour regression.; transfer_boundary: Image fitness uses the gallery asset because Commons results were envelope labels.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured ultrastructural wavelength from Edwards or Werner. | Does not claim nonlinear spot coarsening stays at 2.765 µm. | Does not claim the Lean proofs were checked by a Lean kernel in this environment.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2: continuous δ sweep is panel (2,0) of the comparison figure.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2: orientation KS and Otsu foreground fractions are in measure_morphoeval.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'RESOLVED in pass 2: zero-arm ablation is rendered and its CV drop is a measurement.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'No anatomical 2.8 µm micrograph was available; Commons files were envelope labels. The gallery spiral remains the fitness target.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Lean theorems are sorry-free but were not kernel-checked; lean is not installed in this environment.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.82e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

