<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila grimshawi Turing wavelength at 2.8 µm (detail) (Drosophila grimshawi)",
        "Drosophila grimshawi Turing wavelength at 2.8 µm (detail) faithfully reproduces Drosophila grimshawi morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila grimshawi specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila grimshawi" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured ultrastructural wavelength from Edwards or Werner.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim nonlinear spot coarsening stays at 2.765 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the Lean proofs were checked by a Lean kernel in this environment.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fastest-mode calibration, numerical growth fit, δ sweep, chronoseries order, orientation KS, Otsu fractions, and the zero-arm ablation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spiral render with the specimen radial envelope and a melanin colour regression.",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards et al. (2007) and Werner et al. (2010) are the picture-wing and guttifera Wingless sources. They do not measure a 2.765 µm wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) supply the instability and the kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: Image fitness uses the gallery asset because Commons results were envelope labels." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila grimshawi (Hawaiian Picture-Winged Giant Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-grimshawi-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_grimshawi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila grimshawi; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing (1952) and Schnakenberg (1979) supply the instability and the kinetics. | Edwards et al. (2007) and Werner et al. (2010) are the picture-wing and guttifera Wingless sources. They do not measure a 2.765 µm wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: Fastest-mode calibration, numerical growth fit, δ sweep, chronoseries order, orientation KS, Otsu fractions, and the zero-arm ablation. | Spiral render with the specimen radial envelope and a melanin colour regression.; transfer_boundary: Image fitness uses the gallery asset because Commons results were envelope labels.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured ultrastructural wavelength from Edwards or Werner. | Does not claim nonlinear spot coarsening stays at 2.765 µm. | Does not claim the Lean proofs were checked by a Lean kernel in this environment.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature06341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature08896>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/dgd.12661>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0000487> ;
